-- title:
--   The carry 2-cochain of a cyclic group is a cocycle
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a group and $s\in G$ an element such that every $g\in G$ lies in the subgroup $\mathrm{zpowers}(s)$ of integer powers of $s$, and such that $s$ has finite order; let $A$ be a representation of $G$ over $\mathbb Z$ and let $a\in A$ be fixed by the action of $s$, i.e. $A.\rho(s)\,a = a$. Write $n = \mathrm{orderOf}\,s$ and, for $g\in G$, let $\mathrm{cyclicLog}(g)\in\mathbb N$ be the value in $\{0,\dots,n-1\}$ attached to $g$ by the inverse of Mathlib's bijection `finEquivZPowers` between $\mathrm{Fin}\,n$ and $\mathrm{zpowers}(s)$, that is, the discrete logarithm of $g$ to base $s$ normalised to the range $[0,n)$. The assertion is that the function $G\times G\to A$ given by $(g,h)\mapsto a$ when $n \le \mathrm{cyclicLog}(g)+\mathrm{cyclicLog}(h)$ and $(g,h)\mapsto 0$ otherwise — the "carry" cochain `carryFun s hs hfin a` — belongs to `cocycles₂ A`, i.e. satisfies the inhomogeneous $2$-cocycle identity $A.\rho(g)\,F(h,j) - F(gh,j) + F(g,hj) - F(g,h) = 0$ for all $g,h,j\in G$.
--
--   This is the classical cocycle of a cyclic group: for $G$ cyclic of order $n$ generated by $s$, the carry of the discrete logarithm, multiplied by an $s$-invariant element $a$, is a $2$-cocycle, and its class is the standard generator-type class in $H^2(G,A)$ used for cyclic algebras and for the fundamental class of a cyclic extension. It underlies the local-level statements about the local fundamental class and about $H^2$ of the invariants of unit groups that cite it.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_groupCohomology_carryFun_mem_cocycles2.lean

import Mathlib
